From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0153-guard-clear-uploads-against-lower-left-scissors.patch

Source: 0153-guard-clear-uploads-against-lower-left-scissors.patch
skip, which is 0146 here (Lichii PR 141, Kajcsi).

Vulkan GetScissorState reflects the Y interval around surface_clip.height and
clamps negative bounds to zero. With a lower-left window origin a scissor
whose raw Y interval looks full can clear no rows after that transform.
Require the transformed interval to start at zero and cover the new render
target before suppressing its guest upload; otherwise RefreshContents runs as
before.

Changed from the source: placed inside 0146's use_scissor block, so the
scissor-enable test is the block's own.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
 src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
index d3b60d4800..49e9f15911 100644
--- a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
@@ -3122,6 +3122,15 @@ ImageId TextureCache<P>::JoinImages(const ImageInfo& info, GPUVAddr gpu_addr, DA
                 scissor.max_y < height) {
                 return false;
             }
+            using WindowOrigin = Tegra::Engines::Maxwell3D::Regs::WindowOrigin;
+            if (regs.window_origin.mode != WindowOrigin::Mode::UpperLeft) {
+                // Vulkan flips Y around surface_clip.height, then clamps both bounds to zero.
+                // Require the transformed interval to start at zero and cover the new image.
+                const u32 clip_height = regs.surface_clip.height;
+                if (scissor.max_y < clip_height || clip_height - scissor.min_y < height) {
+                    return false;
+                }
+            }
         }
         // The clear covers the framebuffer's render area, the smallest bound target.
         for (u32 index = 0; index < regs.rt_control.count && index < NUM_RT; ++index) {
